---
title: "forceToggleAttendance (kintai-v3: Admin Single-User Toggle)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_lookup_user: SELECT FROM attendance.users WHERE supabase_auth_user_id = userId
    q_lookup_user --> q_not_found: user not found or error
    q_not_found --> [*]: return {success=false, message='attendance user not found'}
    q_lookup_user --> q_get_last: user found with card_id
    q_get_last --> q_query_last: SELECT type FROM attendances WHERE user_id ORDER BY timestamp DESC LIMIT 1
    q_query_last --> q_query_error: query error (not PGRST116)
    q_query_error --> [*]: return {success=false, message=error}
    q_query_last --> q_determine_type: success or no rows
    q_determine_type --> q_insert: newType = (lastType='in' ? 'out' : 'in')
    q_insert --> q_record: INSERT attendances(user_id, type=newType, card_id, timestamp=now, date=JST)
    q_record --> q_insert_error: insert error
    q_insert_error --> [*]: return {success=false}
    q_record --> q_success: insert success
    q_success --> [*]: revalidatePath, return {success=true, message='forced in/out'}

    note right of q_determine_type
        INV-001: Toggle logic same as normal attendance (in<->out)
        INV-002: No prior-record defaults to 'in' (same as card tap)
        INV-003: Uses admin client (bypasses RLS) - no auth check in function itself
        INV-004: Date computed in Asia/Tokyo timezone
    end note
